  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Four services, three startup shapes",
      "items": [
        "Four services ship here: broker, worker, storage and the tooth-modeling adapter",
        "Three different startup shapes appear across those four binaries",
        "Only the broker and the worker touch the LRO spine at all"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Both halves ride the in-repo spine",
      "items": [
        "The broker imports pkg/postgres-lro, not the external DS-DP-S/postgres-lro module",
        "The worker imports pkg/worker-lro for the same reason",
        "cbct-segmentation is the only other MLE family on the in-repo spine"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "An adapter, not a service of its own",
      "items": [
        "tooth-modeling dials a mesh conversion service and an ATM tooth-modeling service",
        "It accepts both basic service auth and a user JWT, so it fronts two caller classes",
        "It queues nothing and owns no work items, so no Operation is ever created here"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Gaps worth closing",
      "items": [
        "No tmo service appears in the Datadog maps, unlike the nine monitored families",
        "mle-pentest-worker is the only other MLE family with no monitor at all",
        "The sidecar is pinned by build SHA v-3400-23fa9abce, a fourth pinning convention"
      ]
    }
